## 3. AMSP Evolution

In close binary systems such as the LMXBs, matter near the surface of the companion star is transferred to the primary star (the latter is a neutron star in the case of AMSPs) when the companion radius R_{\\rm c} is equal to the Roche lobe size R_{\\rm L}. This size is the distance from the center of the donor star to the inner Lagrangian point, where the gravitational forces from the companion and primary are equal and opposite, and is given by(Paczynski, 1971)

